// The characters of the game, in the order the roster of the fight setup screen shows them.
// Each one has a folder in Assets/sprites/characters with its .ase file in it, which Aseprite opens and the game reads as it is.
// Every tag of the file is an animation by the name of the tag, see Art/tools/build_ase.py for how the files were first put together.
// What the files were made from is in Art/characters, which the game doesn't load and doesn't send to whoever joins.
//
//   pretty_name   what the character is called on screen
//   sprites       its .ase file. A folder with a spritesheet.png and a definition.hor in it (how characters used to come) works as well
//   moves         the files its moves come from. A move in a later file replaces the one of the same name from an earlier one,
//                 so a character can share most of its moves with another and only change a few
//   frame_rate    how many frames a second its art plays at. The moves are timed in frames of the fight (60 a second) whatever this is
//   movement      how it gets about, every number what it really does, in world units and seconds (a fighter is about 30 wide
//                 and 73 tall, a tile 16). There is no drag, a speed is the speed.
//                   walk_speed           how fast it walks
//                   ground_acceleration  how quickly it gets up to that, units a second every second
//                   traction             how quickly it stops on the ground, and what eats a shove or a push
//                   air_speed            how fast it drifts in the air
//                   air_acceleration     how quickly it gets up to that
//                   air_friction         how quickly it slows in the air with nothing held
//                   gravity              how hard it falls, units a second every second
//                   fall_speed           the fastest it falls, and fast_fall_speed the fastest with down pressed past the top of a jump
//                   jump_height          how high a jump gets its feet, short_hop_height a tap of up, double_jump_height one in the air
//                   double_jumps         how many jumps it has in the air
//                   hitstun_gravity      how much of its gravity it falls with in hitstun, half to be juggled (Rivals of Aether has it the same)
//   scale         how big the character is against the others, 1 if left out. Everything scales with it, the sprite, the body and the hitboxes
//   stats         the bars on the fight setup screen, each from 0 to 100. They are only for show,
//                 how a character really plays is up to its moves and the numbers above

